# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>
#
# --- GUIDELINES ---
# Type: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, chore, build, ci
# Scope: Optional component/module (api, core, tests, deps, etc.)
# Subject: Imperative mood, no period, max 50 chars
# Body: Why this change? What does it do? (wrap at 72 chars)
# Footer: Breaking changes, issue refs (e.g., Refs: #123)
#
# --- EXAMPLES ---
#
# Simple one-line commit:
# feat(auth): add JWT token validation
#
# Commit with detailed body:
# fix(evaluator): resolve memory leak in async operations
#
# - Close client connections after each evaluation
# - Add proper cleanup in error handlers
# - Update tests to verify connection management
#
# Refs: #456
#
# Multiple changes in one commit:
# chore: improve development workflow
#
# - Add pre-commit hooks for linting and formatting
# - Update VS Code settings for auto-format on save
# - Configure git commit message template
#
# Breaking change example:
# feat(api)!: change evaluation endpoint response format
#
# BREAKING CHANGE: Response now returns detailed metrics object
# instead of simple score. Update clients to use new format:
# { "score": 0.95, "metrics": {...} }
